WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.456
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03.506 --> 00:00:06.499
Robotics 101, video 1.

3
00:00:06.549 --> 00:00:09.820
Welcome to Robotics 101.

4
00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:12.288
Hello and welcome!

5
00:00:12.338 --> 00:00:16.838
In this course you will build a small robot that can follow

6
00:00:16.888 --> 00:00:20.000
a black line on the floor, all by itself.

7
00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:26.186
Here is the robot you will build, shown in our simulator.

8
00:00:26.236 --> 00:00:30.472
It has two eyes underneath that look at the floor.

9
00:00:30.522 --> 00:00:34.758
When the line bends, the robot turns to follow it.

10
00:00:34.808 --> 00:00:36.644
Nobody is steering it.

11
00:00:36.694 --> 00:00:39.130
The robot decides on its own.

12
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.884
Robots like this are used in real life.

13
00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:50.601
Warehouse robots follow lines to carry parcels.

14
00:00:50.651 --> 00:00:56.217
Some hospitals use them to deliver medicines, and factories use them to

15
00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:59.380
move parts from one machine to the next.

16
00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.409
The course has four modules.

17
00:01:03.459 --> 00:01:06.022
First, you meet your robot.

18
00:01:06.072 --> 00:01:09.409
Next, you learn how its parts work.

19
00:01:09.459 --> 00:01:12.022
Then you write the program.

20
00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:16.860
Finally, you build it, test it and make it better.

21
00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:21.030
Every lesson follows the same pattern.

22
00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:25.797
You watch a short video, try an activity or the simulator, check

23
00:01:25.847 --> 00:01:30.490
what you learned with a few questions, and then build and test.

24
00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:35.542
Do not worry if you do not have a robot kit yet.

25
00:01:35.592 --> 00:01:40.764
Every lesson works in your browser, and the simulator lets you test

26
00:01:40.814 --> 00:01:41.933
the same ideas.

27
00:01:41.983 --> 00:01:47.000
You can even complete the final challenge on the virtual pathway.

28
00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:49.340
Safety first.

29
00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:52.940
Always ask an adult before you use batteries.

30
00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:56.540
Never let the battery wires touch each other.

31
00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:01.900
Unplug the power before you change any wires, and keep your fingers

32
00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:05.820
away from the wheels when the motors are running.

33
00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:12.119
By the end, you will have a working robot, a certificate, and

34
00:02:12.169 --> 00:02:15.080
six badges to collect along the way.

35
00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:16.150
Let us begin!

36
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:18.912
Let us recap.

37
00:02:18.962 --> 00:02:24.045
You will build a robot that follows a black line.

38
00:02:24.095 --> 00:02:28.026
Fifteen short lessons in four modules.

39
00:02:28.076 --> 00:02:28.759
No kit?

40
00:02:28.809 --> 00:02:32.111
The simulator covers every step.

41
00:02:32.161 --> 00:02:36.930
Next: Understanding robots: sense, think, act.
